1
00:00:00,079 --> 00:00:02,019
Beer almost always comes in brown glass,

2
00:00:02,220 --> 00:00:03,679
because light physically breaks beer.

3
00:00:03,939 --> 00:00:05,960
Hops leave compounds in the liquid that are

4
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:06,759
stable in the dark.

5
00:00:07,019 --> 00:00:08,800
Hit them with blue and ultraviolet light,

6
00:00:09,039 --> 00:00:11,439
and riboflavin, a vitamin already in the beer,

7
00:00:11,719 --> 00:00:12,479
acts as a middleman.

8
00:00:12,739 --> 00:00:14,819
It absorbs the light and hands the energy along

9
00:00:14,859 --> 00:00:15,979
until those hop compounds

10
00:00:16,359 --> 00:00:17,940
shatter into something chemically close to

11
00:00:18,039 --> 00:00:18,639
skunk spray.

12
00:00:18,859 --> 00:00:20,299
That is not a figure of speech.

13
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,899
Brown glass blocks nearly all of those wavelengths.

14
00:00:23,239 --> 00:00:25,139
Green blocks a fraction, which is why some

15
00:00:25,199 --> 00:00:26,719
imports taste faintly like a warning.
